    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The purpose of network proxy-related keys in the playbook is to allow Antora to be used behind an HTTP/HTTPS proxy, such as in a typical corporate environment. The requests these keys impact, at present, include those made by the git client in the content aggregator and the HTTP client in the UI loader."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, Antora respects the industry-standard "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "http_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "https_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " environment variables, if set. That means Antora may automatically proxy network requests, even if these keys are not set in the playbook file. This reflects a noteworthy change in behavior from Antora 2."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "http_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "https_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " environment variables specify a URL through which Antora should route HTTP and HTTP requests, respectively. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " environment variable allows for requests to certain domains or subdomains to bypass the proxy (i.e., exclusions)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "It’s not possible to configure different proxies for different URLs using this approach. The only URL-specific configuration is to disable the proxy for certain domains or subdomains using "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By honoring these environment variables, Antora is fulfilling the standard contract in network programming for working with proxies without having to modify the settings at the application level. This is the contract by which network-based software is developed. If the connection still cannot be made when these environment variables are set, it’s an IT issue."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If it’s necessary to configure the proxy settings without the use of environment variables, then, and only then, do you need to specify them in the playbook file. If that’s the case, read on."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "automatic-configuration",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Automatic configuration"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "http_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts a URL through which to route HTTP requests. The URL should only contain the protocol (http or https), domain (root domain or subdomain), and a port. When set, all HTTP requests made by Antora will be routed through this URL."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "network:\n  http_proxy: http://localhost:3128"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The protocol of the proxy URL does not have to match the protocol of the original URL."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "http-proxy",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "http_proxy key"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "https_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts a URL through which to route HTTPS requests. The URL should only contain the protocol (http or https), domain (root domain or subdomain), and a port. When set, all HTTPS requests made by Antora will be routed through this URL."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "network:\n  https_proxy: http://localhost:3128"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The protocol of the proxy URL does not have to match the protocol of the original URL."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "https-proxy",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "https_proxy key"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key specifies proxy exclusions. These exclusions are expressed as a comma-separated list of domains or subdomains. If the URL of a request matches one of these values, it will not be routed through the proxy, even if a proxy is configured for the protocol of the URL (http or https)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "network:\n  no_proxy: gitlab.com,github.com"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To turn off the proxy for all requests, set this value to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "network:\n  no_proxy: '*'"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora 2 didn’t honor the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "http_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "https_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " environment variables. If you’re migrating from Antora 2 to Antora 3, and you encounter a network error (Bad response: 503), the automatic proxy support in Antora 3 may be the culprit. If the proxy is standing in the way of Antora connecting to an endpoint, you may need to bypass the proxy using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "no_proxy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key. If you want to avoid modifying your playbook, you can specify this key using a CLI option:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ antora --noproxy '*' antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "However, if this is necessary, you may want to understand why the proxy is failing to route the request."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "no-proxy",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "no_proxy key"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Network Proxy"
      }
    ]
  }
}
